<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Belek Ghazi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1124">1124</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Balak</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Belek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi">Ghazi</a> was an Artuqid Turkoman emir, a nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilghazi">Ilghazi</a>, who held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harput">Harput</a> and other fortresses in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. In 1122 he captured Joscelin I of the County of Edessa and in 1123 King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-ii-of-jerusalem">Baldwin II of Jerusalem</a>, holding them at Harput, though Joscelin escaped. He took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> in 1123 but was killed in 1124 while besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manbij">Manbij</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belek-ghazi.jpg" alt="Belek Ghazi" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vikiçizer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elaz%C4%B1%C4%9F2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
